# Phase 3 remoting transport work log — 2026-09-27 10:55:36 UTC

## Scope
Repair the GO_AWAY retry race found during Phase 3 transport review. Java 5.5.1 remains the client behavior baseline. Phase 3 is not accepted or complete; P3-V04 remains deferred to Phase 19; Phase 4 is not started.

## Changes
- Fixed `retire_for_go_away` so a GO_AWAY response can still initiate the one allowed retry if the old socket has already closed and its active cache entry was removed. The retired-generation marker is preserved while the connection remains alive, so a second response on that generation cannot initiate another retry.
- Prevented retirement/retry when a replacement is already cached for that address, and made connection-close bookkeeping remove the current/retired generation under a consistent pair of locks. A retired close no longer removes or closes a replacement.
- Added `p3_multiple_go_away_responses_on_retired_connection_only_retry_once`, exercising two in-flight requests on the old channel, one replacement/retry, and a second GO_AWAY response from the retired generation.
- Updated the compatibility inventory's GO_AWAY and signed-time entries to record the latest reviewed behavior and evidence.

